---
layout: base.njk
title: Message sent
noindex: true
description: "Your message reached the Prospektor inbox. We read it and reply by email, to the address you gave. Nothing else happens with it."
# One page per language (#535): /contact/ posts to the twin in its own
# language, so this has to exist wherever /contact/ does.
pagination:
  data: languages
  size: 1
  alias: language
  addAllPagesToCollections: true
permalink: "{{ language.prefix }}/contact/thanks/"
---

{#- #456. Netlify Forms redirects here after a successful POST from /contact/,
    so this URL has to be one the build really writes: netlify.toml ends in a
    /* → /404.html catch-all, and the success page is fetched as an ordinary
    request once the POST is handled. test/contact.test.js pins the form's
    action to a built file for exactly that reason.

    noindex, and deliberately out of the sitemap: it is the /checkout/done/
    case — thin, transactional, and meaningless to anyone who arrives at it
    cold. It answers no search. One primary action, back to the product. -#}

<header class="page-hero">
  <div class="page-hero-inner">
    <span class="tag">{% t %}contact{% endt %}</span>
    <h1 class="page-h1">{% t %}Message sent.{% endt %}</h1>
    <p class="page-lede">
      {% t %}It's in our inbox. We reply by email, to the address you gave.{% endt %}
    </p>
    <a class="btn-cta" href="{{ '/' | localize }}">{% t %}Back to Prospektor{% endt %}</a>
  </div>
</header>
